        "description": "<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">You're a data analyst at \"SkyTravel Airlines\". The operations team needs to analyze flight delay patterns. They provide you with flight data and ask:&nbsp;\"Can you show each flight's delay along with the next flight's delay from the same route for comparison?\"</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The&nbsp;<strong>'flights'</strong>&nbsp;table contains columns&nbsp;<strong>'flight_id'</strong>&nbsp;(primary key),&nbsp;<strong>'route'</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>'departure_time'</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>'delay_minutes'</strong>&nbsp;(positive = delayed, negative = early).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\"><strong>Your task is to:</strong><br />For each flight, display its delay alongside the&nbsp;<strong>next flight's delay</strong>&nbsp;on the same route (ordered by departure time).</p>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The output columns should Include <strong>'flight_id'</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>'route'</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>'delay_minutes'</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>'next_flight_delay'</strong>, ordered by&nbsp;<strong>'route'</strong>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<strong>'departure_time'</strong>.</p>",
