        "title": "Chasing the Haze",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p class=\"\" data-start=\"317\" data-end=\"732\">You recently joined a global climate research group tracking air pollution in major cities. As part of your first assignment, your team is reviewing PM2.5 levels&mdash;fine inhalable particles harmful to lungs&mdash;logged daily across different regions. The focus is on identifying which cities experienced the most dangerous pollution spike in the second week of May 2025, so awareness campaigns can be organized immediately.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"895\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"895\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"895\">The 'air_quality' table contains the columns 'record_id', 'city', 'pm25_level', and 'reading_date'. Each row logs the PM2.5 level of a city on a specific date.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"913\">Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"1014\">Identify the city that had the highest recorded PM2.5 level between '2025-05-08' and '2025-05-15'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"1017\" data-end=\"1108\">Retrieve all records for that city from the same date range to study the pollution pattern.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1226\"><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">The </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">output </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">columns </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">should </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">be '</span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">city', '</span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">reading_date', </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">and '</span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">pm25_level', </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">ordered </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">by '</span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">reading_date' </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">in </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">ascending </span><span class=\"_fadeIn_4f9by_7\">order.</span></p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE air_quality (\n  record_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  city VARCHAR(100),\n  pm25_level DECIMAL(5,2),\n  reading_date DATE\n);\nINSERT INTO air_quality VALUES\n  (101, 'Beijing', 300.00, '2025-05-09'),\n  (102, 'Shanghai', 220.50, '2025-05-10'),\n  (103, 'Beijing', 310.10, '2025-05-11'),\n  (104, 'Seoul', 170.00, '2025-05-12'),\n  (105, 'Shanghai', 280.20, '2025-05-14'),\n  (106, 'Beijing', 305.60, '2025-05-15');",
