        "id": "573662",
        "title": "Elite Hackers",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>The hacker group tracks members by their successful hack counts. Leadership requires identifying the second most prolific hackers to allocate advanced resources, handling ties inclusively. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given one table: 'hackers': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'hackers' table includes the columns 'hacker_id', 'hacker_alias', and 'hack_count', representing unique hacker identifiers, hacker aliases, and total successful hacks. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that identifies the hackers who hold the second-highest hack count.</p>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'hacker_alias' and 'hack_count', ordered by hacker_alias in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE hackers (\n    hacker_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    hacker_alias VARCHAR(50),\n    hack_count INT\n);\nINSERT INTO hackers VALUES\n(1, 'Phantom', 150),\n(2, 'Spectre', 200),\n(3, 'Ghost', 150),\n(4, 'Wraith', 180),\n(5, 'Void', 200);\n\n",
        "slug": "elite-hackers",
