        "title": "Interplanetary Procrastinators",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p class=\"\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"452\">The interplanetary comms crackled with frustration as Colony Director Cho slammed her space-gloved fist on the desk. Another delayed shipment of hydroponic seeds had arrived with a terse note: \"Solar storm reroute.\" This was the third time this month. She turned to you, the colony's newest logistics analyst, with a mission&mdash;find the most egregiously late shipments in each category, but only those with sufficiently detailed explanations to justify their tardiness.</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"454\" data-end=\"505\">You are given two tables: &lsquo;shipments&rsquo; and &lsquo;delays&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"509\" data-end=\"679\">The &lsquo;shipments&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;shipment_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;supply_type&rsquo;, and &lsquo;description&rsquo;. &lsquo;shipment_id&rsquo; is primary key; each row details what was sent and a text note on content.</li>\n<li data-start=\"682\" data-end=\"837\">The &lsquo;delays&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;shipment_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;delay_days&rsquo;. &lsquo;shipment_id&rsquo; references &lsquo;shipments&rsquo;, and each row records how many days the shipment was late.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"839\" data-end=\"1006\">Your task is to identify, for each supply_type, the two shipments with the greatest delay_days whose description length exceeds the overall average description length.</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1008\" data-end=\"1168\">The output columns should be &lsquo;shipment_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;supply_type&rsquo;, &lsquo;delay_days&rsquo;, and &lsquo;description&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;supply_type&rsquo; ascending, then by &lsquo;delay_days&rsquo; descending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE shipments (\n  shipment_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  supply_type VARCHAR(50),\n  description TEXT\n);\nCREATE TABLE delays (\n  shipment_id INT,\n  delay_days INT\n);\nINSERT INTO shipments VALUES\n  (1, 'Food', 'Fresh produce and staples for daily meals.'),\n  (2, 'Medicine', 'Antibiotics and pain relievers.'),\n  (3, 'Equipment', 'Repair tools and replacement parts.'),\n  (4, 'Food', 'Dehydrated fruit and high-energy bars.'),\n  (5, 'Medicine', 'Vaccines requiring cold storage.'),\n  (6, 'Equipment', 'Heavy-duty drilling apparatus.');\nINSERT INTO delays VALUES\n  (1, 5),\n  (2, 2),\n  (3, 7),\n  (4, 10),\n  (5, 8),\n  (6, 3);",
        "slug": "interplanetary-procrastinators",
