        "id": "570717",
        "title": "Silver Lighthouse Tours",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"146\">As the lead analyst for Coastal Getaways, you were handed an urgent request from the VP of Sales to promote our mid-tier performing tours&mdash;not the top sellers that market themselves, but the hidden gems ranked below the top tour. The goal was to boost underrated lighthouse experiences before peak travel season.</p>\n<p data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"146\">You are given two tables, 'tours' and 'sales', that contain information about tour packages and their respective sales.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"150\" data-end=\"321\">The 'tours' table includes the columns 'tour_id', 'resort', and 'lighthouse', representing each tour's identifier, the resort name, and the lighthouse destination.</li>\n<li data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"465\">The 'sales' table includes the columns 'sale_id', 'tour_id', and 'sale_amount', where each row represents a sale for a specific tour.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"619\">Write a query to identify the next highest-grossing tours among those offered at the resorts 'Alpine Ridge', 'Frost Peak', or 'Crystal Bay'.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"623\" data-end=\"709\">Calculate the total revenue for each qualifying tour using the sum of 'sale_amount'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"712\" data-end=\"788\">Include tours that may not have any sales (i.e., their revenue should be 0).</li>\n<li data-start=\"791\" data-end=\"862\">Rank the tours based on descending total revenue and ascending tour ID.</li>\n<li data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"912\">Select only the tours ranked 2nd, 3rd, and 4th.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"914\" data-end=\"1053\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The final output should include columns 'resort', 'lighthouse', and 'total_revenue', sorted by 'total_revenue' in descending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE tours (\n  tour_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  resort VARCHAR(100),\n  lighthouse VARCHAR(100)\n);\nCREATE TABLE sales (\n  sale_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  tour_id INT,\n  sale_amount DECIMAL(10,2)\n);\nINSERT INTO tours VALUES\n  (1, 'Alpine Ridge', 'North Beacon'),\n  (2, 'Frost Peak',   'East Beacon'),\n  (3, 'Crystal Bay',  'South Beacon'),\n  (4, 'Timberline',   'West Beacon');\nINSERT INTO sales VALUES\n  (1, 1, 500.00),\n  (2, 1, 250.00),\n  (3, 2, 400.00),\n  (4, 2, 300.00),\n  (5, 3, 350.00),\n  (6, 3, 200.00),\n  (7, 4, 450.00);\n\n",
