        "description": "<p>Gold rush towns track miners' productivity in desert canyon mines. Investors require performance rankings to allocate bonuses for top miners in specific canyon mines with mathematically significant vein sizes. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'gold_mines' and 'miners': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'gold_mines' table includes the columns 'mine_id', 'mine_name', 'region', and 'vein_size', representing unique mine identifiers, mine names, desert regions, and gold vein sizes (integer units). &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'miners' table includes the columns 'miner_id', 'miner_name', 'mine_id', 'shifts_worked', and 'gold_found_grams', representing unique miner identifiers, miner names, mine IDs, total shifts worked, and gold extracted in grams. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Filters for mines in regions containing &ldquo;Canyon&rdquo; with a vein_size divisible by 3.</li>\n<li>Calculates each miner&rsquo;s gold_per_shift as gold_found_grams divided by shifts_worked.</li>\n<li>Ranks miners within each mine by gold_per_shift in descending order.</li>\n<li>Selects only the top-ranked miner (ranking = 1) for each mine.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'mine_name', 'miner_name', 'gold_per_shift', and 'ranking', ordered by mine_name in ascending order and gold_per_shift in descending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE gold_mines (\n    mine_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    mine_name VARCHAR(50),\n    region VARCHAR(50),\n    vein_size INT\n);\nINSERT INTO gold_mines VALUES\n(5, 'Lucky Shot', 'Copper Canyon', 15),\n(6, 'Sunburst', 'Mojave Desert', 4),\n(7, 'Canyon Gem', 'Blue Canyon', 21),\n(8, 'Bonanza', 'Iron Canyon', 18);\n\nCREATE TABLE miners (\n    miner_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    miner_name VARCHAR(50),\n    mine_id INT,\n    shifts_worked INT,\n    gold_found_grams DECIMAL(8,2)\n);\nINSERT INTO miners VALUES\n(201, 'Roy Blake', 5, 40, 320.00),\n(202, 'Sally Grey', 5, 35, 315.00),\n(203, 'Otis Reed', 7, 20, 210.00),\n(204, 'Mae Wells', 7, 20, 210.00),\n(205, 'Ned Shaw', 8, 25, 200.00),\n(206, 'Ivy Stone', 8, 30, 270.00);\n\n",
        "slug": "prospector-performance-rankings",
