        "description": "<p class=\"\" data-start=\"178\" data-end=\"221\">The Meteorological Department is monitoring an unprecedented heatwave sweeping across the country. With temperatures soaring and UV radiation reaching dangerous levels, the MD needs to identify cities under prolonged extreme weather conditions to issue public health alerts.</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"178\" data-end=\"221\">Your task is to analyze weather data for this you are given a table 'weather_readings'.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"435\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"435\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"225\" data-end=\"435\">The 'weather_readings' table includes the columns 'city', 'reading_date', 'peak_temperature', and 'peak_uv_index'. Each row represents the recorded weather data for a specific city on a specific date.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"437\" data-end=\"624\">The system assigns alerts based on peak daily temperature and peak UV index readings per city.<br data-start=\"531\" data-end=\"534\" />An alert is raised only if conditions persist for at least 3 consecutive days or more.</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"739\">For at least 3 consecutive days, assign the highest applicable alert level based on the following conditions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"743\" data-end=\"812\"><strong>🔴 </strong>Red Alert: peak_temperature &ge; 44 AND peak_uv_index &ge; 11</li>\n<li data-start=\"815\" data-end=\"885\"><strong>🟠 </strong>Orange Alert: peak_temperature &ge; 42 (UV index does not matter)</li>\n<li data-start=\"888\" data-end=\"959\"><strong>🟡 </strong>Yellow Alert: peak_temperature &ge; 40 AND peak_uv_index &ge; 8</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For each such period, calculate the start_date, end_date, the average values of peak_temperature and peak_uv_index rounded to one decimal place.</p>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'city', 'start_date', 'end_date', 'alert_level' (Red/Orange/Yellow), 'avg_temp', and 'avg_uv_index', ordered by city and start_date in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE weather_readings (\n  city VARCHAR(50),\n  reading_date DATE,\n  peak_temperature DECIMAL(4,1),\n  peak_uv_index DECIMAL(3,1)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO weather_readings VALUES\n('Delhi', '2025-05-01', 45.0, 12.0),\n('Delhi', '2025-05-02', 44.5, 11.5),\n('Delhi', '2025-05-03', 44.6, 11.0),\n('Delhi', '2025-05-07', 44.6, 11.0),\n('Bhopal', '2025-05-10', 42.0, 9.0),\n('Bhopal', '2025-05-11', 42.1, 8.5),\n('Bhopal', '2025-05-12', 43.0, 10.0),\n('Nagpur', '2025-05-05', 40.5, 8.0),\n('Nagpur', '2025-05-06', 41.0, 8.5),\n('Nagpur', '2025-05-07', 40.2, 8.3),\n('Nagpur', '2025-05-08', 39.9, 7.8);",
